<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:36:27 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Canaries urge government action after 2,200 migrants reach the islands in 48h</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261115-canaries-urge-government-action-after-2-200-migrants-reach-the-islands-in-48h-1</link><description>
Spain says nearly 2,200 migrants have arrived by boat to the Canary Islands this weekend. The Spanish islands are one of the main entry points into Europe for migrants from Africa. The Spanish Interior Ministry says more than 13,000 arrived there between January and the end of last month. Details and analysis by Andrew Hilliar, FRANCE 24 international affairs editor.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6524e48c-e108-11f1-a387-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-160718-161132-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6524e48c-e108-11f1-a387-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-160718-161132-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6a1a4c02-e108-11f1-ad35-f165ee9aaa0a</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:24:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Santa school in full swing in London ahead of Christmas celebrations</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/santa-school-in-full-swing-in-london-ahead-of-christmas-celebrations</link><description>
It may still be November but it's beginning to look a lot like Christmas in South London, as many Santa impersonators are heading to school for their festive training. The school, organised by an event company called Ministry of Fun, brings together Santas, elves, and Mrs Clauses to share experiences, practice belly laughs and learn how to bring the magic of Christmas to life. Story by Rachael Griffiths.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c9d5d0c4-e100-11f1-b165-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-082508-082646-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c9d5d0c4-e100-11f1-b165-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-082508-082646-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cea94b12-e100-11f1-8159-af3882b07dd6</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:35:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>The week in pictures: Spain protests, Pope Leo's Peru 'homecoming' and Rocky fans in Philly</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261115-the-week-in-pictures-spain-protests-pope-leo-peru-homecoming-rocky-fans-philly-rosalia</link><description>
FRANCE 24 looks back at some of the week's most striking images, from angry protests over a housing crisis that has dominated Spain's election campaign, to Leo XIV's visit to his adopted homeland Peru and "Rocky" fans marking 50 years since the release of boxing movie classic.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c94a7240-e01f-11f1-b658-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26317808141916.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c94a7240-e01f-11f1-b658-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26317808141916.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0bb2340c-e04c-11f1-87ef-f38af753107f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:59:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c94a7240-e01f-11f1-b658-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26317808141916.jpg">© Matt Slocum, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ukrainian drones strike Russia's petrochemical capital in overnight assault</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261115-ukrainian-drones-strike-russia-s-petrochemical-capital-in-overnight-assault</link><description>
Russian officials confirmed Sunday that the central industrial city of Nizhnekamsk had endured "prolonged" Ukrainian airstrikes overnight, damaging a residential building and sparking a fire at a major petrochemical complex, injuring three people. Separate overnight strikes on Taganrog city killed an electricity substation engineer, according to the regional governor.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ffd45668-e0f2-11f1-b056-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-10T121054Z-860283693-RC2QMNADH8MD-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-RUSSIA-OIL-REFINING.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ffd45668-e0f2-11f1-b056-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-10T121054Z-860283693-RC2QMNADH8MD-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-RUSSIA-OIL-REFINING.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6f78b640-e0f2-11f1-bbc2-4d5422d2da01</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:36:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ffd45668-e0f2-11f1-b056-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-10T121054Z-860283693-RC2QMNADH8MD-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-RUSSIA-OIL-REFINING.jpg">© Stringer, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Will Ukraine make territorial concessions for NATO membership?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/will-ukraine-make-territorial-concessions-for-nato-membership</link><description>
The United States suggested Ukraine make territorial concessions in exchange for a NATO membership, according to Volodymyr Zelensky. The Ukrainian president also claims that Russia has rejected an energy truce. This week’s US-mediated negotiations did not result in any tangible progress. Story by Simon Moritz.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a2d6cf0e-e0ed-11f1-b351-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-100632-100811-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a2d6cf0e-e0ed-11f1-b351-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-100632-100811-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a8efcd00-e0ed-11f1-aa8c-d536873720f8</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:14:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Macron says limiting Ukraine aid would pave way to 'another war'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261114-macron-says-limiting-ukraine-aid-would-pave-way-to-another-war</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron on Saturday warned that limiting aid to Ukraine would force Kyiv into an "unjust peace" and risk another war. His statement comes as the United States pushes ahead with efforts to negotiate between Ukraine and Moscow.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b003a0ce-ce6b-11f1-a0f5-23d55109f116/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26295395173953-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b003a0ce-ce6b-11f1-a0f5-23d55109f116/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26295395173953-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e7c51666-e066-11f1-9276-8d5f824b8502</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:15:43 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b003a0ce-ce6b-11f1-a0f5-23d55109f116/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26295395173953-1.jpg">© Teresa Suarez, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Who are the 'street medics' showing up at protests around the world?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/who-are-the-street-medics-showing-up-at-protests-around-the-world</link><description>
From treating tear gas exposure to tending to injuries, street medics have become an increasingly common sight at protests all over the world. But who exactly are they and when did they start showing up at demonstrations? Story by Daniel Quinlan.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/764618c8-e025-11f1-878e-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d4ac3443.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/764618c8-e025-11f1-878e-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d4ac3443.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">405d92aa-e01f-11f1-9579-21782230ef7c</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:19:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>US proposed Ukraine cedes Donbas in exchange for joining NATO, Zelensky says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261114-us-negotiators-suggest-ukraine-cedes-territory-in-exchange-for-nato-membership</link><description>
President Zelensky said the US had proposed ceding Ukraine's eastern city of Donbas to Russia, in exchange for Ukrainian membership of NATO, following the latest round of peace talks in Abu Dhabi this week. He reiterated that Kyiv was not willing to retreat from its territory and warned that the Kremlin's bid to change the continent's security architecture could lead to more wars. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/70cfdcca-e012-11f1-8f8f-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26316802067115.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/70cfdcca-e012-11f1-8f8f-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26316802067115.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0675832e-e013-11f1-8769-fbca886990f0</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:30:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/70cfdcca-e012-11f1-8f8f-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26316802067115.jpg">© Peter Morrison, AP Photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>France among five major powers to represent EU in Ukraine talks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261113-europe-to-send-diplomats-from-across-the-continent-to-ukraine-peace-talks</link><description>
European Council President Antonio Costa on Friday said that Brussels will send diplomats from the bloc and five countries, including the UK, France, Germany, Italy and Poland, to upcoming Ukraine talks. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b484b08c-dfa7-11f1-aaa1-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-16T084030Z-885766991-RC274OADTRVQ-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-EU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b484b08c-dfa7-11f1-aaa1-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-16T084030Z-885766991-RC274OADTRVQ-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-EU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eb2163f8-dfa5-11f1-905e-2757b17c2537</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:38:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b484b08c-dfa7-11f1-aaa1-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-16T084030Z-885766991-RC274OADTRVQ-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-EU.jpg">© Yves Herman, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The World This Week</category><title><![CDATA[The Downfall of AI’s ‘Rock Star’ Boss, Ukraine: Who speaks for Europe? Protests & Presidents]]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261113-the-downfall-of-ai-s-rock-star-boss-ukraine-who-speak-for-europe-protests-presidents</link><description>
On The World This Week with Gavin Lee, our panel distills the breaking news and global stories of the past 7 days into 45 minutes. 
 
Ukraine: Who will speak for Europe?
 
In a week thats seen the first direct talks between Ukraine and Russia since February, with the US in the room and the Europeans relegated to the lobby according to Moscow. A new ‘European Security Architecture’ is discussed.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd993a00-df97-11f1-a921-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/c225d164-32c2-48f7-924f-e100efad3094.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd993a00-df97-11f1-a921-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/c225d164-32c2-48f7-924f-e100efad3094.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6a6ceeda-df91-11f1-81a2-d377275bd746</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:46:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Hurry up and wait: Europe wants a place at the table, ‘must make up its mind’ over Ukraine</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261113-hurry-up-and-wait-europe-wants-a-place-at-the-table-must-make-up-its-mind-over-ukraine</link><description>
Gavin Lee is pleased to welcome Alexander Titov, Lecturer in Modern European History at Queen's University Belfast and a specialist on Russia. He's joined us to discuss high-level meetings in Abu Dhabi, Dublin and the prospects for ending the war in Ukraine.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7839d154-df8c-11f1-9864-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261113-182803-183830-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7839d154-df8c-11f1-9864-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261113-182803-183830-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e238ed08-df94-11f1-ac53-65b57fc79905</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:03:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>'We have done all our homework' to get EU candidate status: Kosovo's PM Albin Kurti</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261113-we-have-done-all-our-homework-to-get-eu-candidate-status-kosovo-s-pm-albin-kurti</link><description>
FRANCE 24 hosts Albin Kurti, the prime minister of Kosovo, a country that declared its independence from Serbia back in 2008 and sees itself as part of the European family. But four years after applying to join the EU, Kosovo has still not received candidate status. We explore Kosovo's path towards the EU, and the broader European and regional dynamics surrounding that.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/419fc3dc-df4c-11f1-8b89-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5e8d4fca.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/419fc3dc-df4c-11f1-8b89-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5e8d4fca.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3b9febd0-dd0b-11f1-944a-9f895a28bed6</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:46:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>As EU grapples with fierce AI competition, summit overshadowed by elusive Ukraine-Russia peace deal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-as-eu-grapples-with-fierce-ai-competition-summit-overshadowed-by-elusive-ukraine-russia-peace-deal-1</link><description>
As EU leaders meet for an AI summit in Dublin, largely overshadowed by Russia's war on Ukraine, William Hilderbrandt is pleased to welcome Fabrice Pothier, CEO of Rasmussen Global. On AI, Pothier points to Europe's limited computing capacity, estimating that it barely represents "5% of what's available out there." Despite the EU's wealth of researchers and expertise, he warns that Europe is struggling to turn these resources into "real technological and industrial scale." Now, turning to the war in Ukraine, Pothier argues that European governments should focus less on "whether they have a place at the table" and more on "making Ukraine's hands stronger," particularly by providing additional air defence interceptors.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/025bc748-df83-11f1-9f2b-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261113-130829-131531-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/025bc748-df83-11f1-9f2b-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261113-130829-131531-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">07f29178-df83-11f1-ac3e-33bf86c9fb30</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:28:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>November 13 Paris attacks: Eleven years later, France pays tribute to victims</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/november-13-paris-attacks-eleven-years-later-france-pays-tribute-to-victims</link><description>
Eleven years on, France pays tribute to the victims of the November 13 attacks. French officials, victims’ associations and families gathered this Friday to pay their respects to those killed in the attacks in Paris on November 13, 2015.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bbb382e2-df80-11f1-a783-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-Thumbnail-5.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bbb382e2-df80-11f1-a783-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-Thumbnail-5.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ccbe977a-df80-11f1-a7dd-67e2ec0fa015</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:47:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>West Bank: ‘Without international trade and financial support, large settlements would not exist’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-west-bank-without-international-trade-and-financial-support-large-settlements-would-not-exist-1</link><description>
France is considering legislation to restrict trade with Israeli settlements in the occupied Palestinian territories, namely the West Bank. Ivar Ekeland, Professor Emeritus at Paris Dauphine-PSL University and Chair of the Organization of Academics for the Respect of International Law in Palestine, discusses the proposed measures with Alison Sargent. He calls for restrictions to cover n ot only goods but also services, including financial services, insurance and tourism. "Without the support of financial entities, of insurance, of providing goods and so on, settlements, big settlements, would not exist," he argues.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7d3f7e80-df7b-11f1-aba2-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261113-080847-081941-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7d3f7e80-df7b-11f1-aba2-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261113-080847-081941-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8270b5ae-df7b-11f1-9261-bb9885e86514</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:15:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russia strikes targets across Ukraine as Kyiv launches nearly 1,200 drones</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-russian-airstrikes-continue-ukraine-launches-nearly-1-200-drones</link><description>
Russian strikes hit targets across Ukraine on Thursday, with one attack damaging a hospital. Ukraine meanwhile fired almost 1,200 drones at Russian targets overnight in one of its biggest aerial attacks since Moscow’s full-scale invasion nearly five years ago.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ac93ac9c-df76-11f1-8215-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8765e4ad.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ac93ac9c-df76-11f1-8215-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8765e4ad.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2a57088c-df76-11f1-b765-1fb5326ddfbf</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:46:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The 51%</category><title>UK rocked by comedians' sex scandals</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261113-uk-rocked-by-comedians-sex-scandals</link><description>
The UK is facing a reckoning in the world of entertainment, as two well-known comedy figures find themselves at the centre of serious allegations and headlines. This as Russell Brand is jailed for more than 10 years after being found guilty of rape and sexual assault and David Walliams faces serious allegations of sexual misconduct.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5ee0506-df60-11f1-91c0-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/brand-walliams.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5ee0506-df60-11f1-91c0-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/brand-walliams.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b1d00012-deb2-11f1-8f4b-07dcda441128</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:47:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Annette YOUNG</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US, Ukraine say Europe to join peace talks as Putin sticks to hardline stance</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-us-ukraine-say-europe-to-join-peace-talks-as-putin-sticks-to-hardline-stance</link><description>
Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky and US envoy Jared Kushner said Thursday, November 12, Europe would join the next round of talks with Russia, as Vladimir Putin indicated Moscow will not compromise on its hardline demands to end almost five years of war. In a packed day of shuttle diplomacy following negotiations in Abu Dhabi, Kushner and fellow envoy Steve Witkoff held over four hours of talks with Putin in the Kremlin before jetting to debrief Zelensky in Dublin.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/da448e3a-df4f-11f1-9d2a-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4c0c2d8a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/da448e3a-df4f-11f1-9d2a-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4c0c2d8a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b866ccbc-df4d-11f1-83ac-a120c5de0d08</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:59:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Winter is coming: Putin seeks to 'hammer Ukrainians, their power grid, their water supplies'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/winter-is-coming-putin-seeks-to-hammer-ukrainians-their-power-grid-their-water-supplies</link><description>
As renewed diplomatic efforts seek to bring an end to Russia's war on Ukraine, the prospect of a negotiated settlement remains unlikely due to Russia's irreconcilable territorial demands, competing visions of European security and an increasingly unpredictable and pro-Moscow US. For Mark Galeotti, Executive Director of Mayak Intelligence and Honorary Professor at University College London's School of Slavonic and East European Studies, Moscow's maximalist vision conceals a more complex negotiating strategy. And the territorial dispute over Donbas presents a particularly formidable obstacle. Putin's determination to claim control over the entirety of the region confronts Ukraine's refusal to surrender territory it continues to hold.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/64f9ee20-df42-11f1-8bdb-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261112-151425-152330-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/64f9ee20-df42-11f1-8bdb-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261112-151425-152330-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6b46e210-df42-11f1-b32a-bddd65b33045</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:26:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Europe to send diplomats from across the continent to Ukraine peace talks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261113-live-zelensky-and-kushner-confirm-that-europe-will-join-next-round-of-russia-ukraine-talks</link><description>
EU leaders on Friday chose five major powers, including France, Britain, Germany, Italy and Poland, to represent European institutions at the next Ukraine talks. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c5b81ec4-d3af-11f1-94da-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-16T085801Z-1180937654-RC284OA1JXI9-RTRMADP-3-EU-SUMMIT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c5b81ec4-d3af-11f1-94da-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-16T085801Z-1180937654-RC284OA1JXI9-RTRMADP-3-EU-SUMMIT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7d7314f8-deee-11f1-9cec-ab45e2195d29</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:39:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c5b81ec4-d3af-11f1-94da-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-16T085801Z-1180937654-RC284OA1JXI9-RTRMADP-3-EU-SUMMIT.jpg">© Stéphanie Lecocq, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>Russia using 'illegal and unethical means, knows Europe won't use same means back', expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261112-russia-using-illegal-and-unethical-means-knows-europe-won-t-use-same-means-back-expert-says</link><description>
There are mounting concerns across Europe that recent hoax threats and cyberattacks could be part of a massive hybrid warfare campaign. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Elisabeth Braw, Senior Fellow with the Atlantic Council’s Transatlantic Security Initiative. She says that Russia's aim is to "increase its power at the expense of European countries and the easiest way to do that is to constantly wage this dirty war against European countries, using illegal and unethical means, because Russia knows that we are not going to use the same means back".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9aecad84-df96-11f1-8db1-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a13c4d91.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9aecad84-df96-11f1-8db1-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a13c4d91.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">245c7212-dee7-11f1-ba78-d1df06cbd525</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:19:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sharon GAFFNEY</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russia using 'illegal and unethical means, knows Europe won't use same means back', expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/russia-using-illegal-and-unethical-means-knows-europe-won-t-use-same-means-back-expert-says</link><description>
There are mounting concerns across Europe that recent hoax threats and cyberattacks could be part of a massive hybrid warfare campaign. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Elisabeth Braw, Senior Fellow with the Atlantic Council’s Transatlantic Security Initiative. She says that Russia's aim is to "increase its power at the expense of European countries and the easiest way to do that is to constantly wage this dirty war against European countries, using illegal and unethical means, because Russia knows that we are not going to use the same means back".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9aecad84-df96-11f1-8db1-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a13c4d91.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9aecad84-df96-11f1-8db1-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a13c4d91.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">68337cee-dee5-11f1-b754-1b093dc5fd5b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:12:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Mauritania fishing boats falsely portrayed as migrant fleet bound for Spain</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261112-mauritania-fishing-boats-falsely-portrayed-as-migrant-fleet-bound-for-spain</link><description>
Spain's Canary Islands are facing renewed pressure from migrant arrivals, with local authorities declaring a state of emergency. Against this backdrop, a viral video claims to show thousands of boats in Mauritania amassing at the port, with users saying they were "ready to set sail" to carry migrants to the archipelago. But the satellite images are misleading: they show a traditional fishing port, not a fleet of migrant vessels. Vedika Bahl explains in Truth or Fake. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc117dca-dee3-11f1-af98-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/canaries.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc117dca-dee3-11f1-af98-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/canaries.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e8f45760-dee3-11f1-bbe6-07473b51b2e7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:56:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Zelensky warns Europe over US-Russia talks on broader security arrangements</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/zelensky-warns-europe-over-us-russia-talks-on-broader-security-arrangements</link><description>
Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky warned European leaders Thursday to be wary of discussions between the United States and Russia about a new security arrangement for the continent. Before launching the war in 2022, the Kremlin delivered an ultimatum to NATO on Europe's security arrangements which included demands for the alliance to withdraw forces from eastern Europe and stop accepting new members. FRANCE 24's Caroline Baum reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eb157cac-ded1-11f1-b7cf-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261112-201030-201228-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eb157cac-ded1-11f1-b7cf-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261112-201030-201228-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f04e1dfa-ded1-11f1-bc1f-9dad418e8b43</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:53:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russia's Vladimir Putin suggests no Ukraine compromise in meeting with US envoys</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-russia-s-vladimir-putin-suggests-no-ukraine-compromise-in-meeting-with-us-envoys</link><description>
Russia's President Vladimir Putin indicated on Thursday, November 12, that the Kremlin would not compromise on its hardline demands to end the war in Ukraine, but offered a short-term ceasefire in a key frontline city during a meeting with US envoys. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e9642f2-deb7-11f1-b9bd-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-38e7cc3a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e9642f2-deb7-11f1-b9bd-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-38e7cc3a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dca321bc-deb6-11f1-a549-63495a9c8bee</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:46:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France: Five men on trial for murder of anti-drug activist Amine Kessaci's brother</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-france-five-men-on-trial-for-murder-of-anti-drug-activist-amine-kessaci-s-brother</link><description>
In France, the trial of five men accused of murdering the brother of anti-drug activist Amine Kessaci is under way. Amine Kessaci, originally known as an environmental activist, became a prominent figure in the fight against drug-related crime after losing two of his brothers to violence linked to drug trafficking. The defendants face the possibility of life imprisonment. The verdict is expected on Monday, November 16. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Angela Diffley tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/77d5cb42-dea0-11f1-93c9-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6c97fb3d.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/77d5cb42-dea0-11f1-93c9-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6c97fb3d.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8368e594-de9f-11f1-9aea-396cd83c3cb0</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:20:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>European leaders gather in Dublin to discuss Ukraine's security, and their own</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-european-leaders-gather-in-dublin-to-discuss-ukraine-s-security-and-their-own</link><description>
Leaders from more than 40 European countries gathered in Dublin on Thursday, November 12, for a summit focused on the continent’s fragile security, amid a new US-backed effort to revive talks on ending the Russia-Ukraine war. The meeting of the European Political Community brought together heads of state and government from European countries and the UK, as well as Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney and NATO Secretary-General Mark Rutte.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a10168be-de82-11f1-acfb-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261112-110426-110630-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a10168be-de82-11f1-acfb-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261112-110426-110630-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a67585a0-de82-11f1-b61d-bf62b6ae6e92</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:19:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Thousands of schools evacuated in Italy as bomb threats spread across Europe</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-thousands-of-schools-evacuated-in-italy-as-bomb-threats-spread-across-europe</link><description>
Schools were evacuated across Italy on Wednesday following a series of hoax bomb threats, but Italian Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni said there was no "concrete danger". The threats come after a series of hoax bomb alerts across Europe in recent weeks, which have prompted growing concern about the possibility of an escalation in hybrid warfare.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eddd5024-de84-11f1-be45-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-ba7e473d.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eddd5024-de84-11f1-be45-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-ba7e473d.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">11b95f8a-de83-11f1-86d8-6d636dfb31ee</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:08:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>COP31: Climate disruption puts farmers and global food supplies under pressure</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-cop31-climate-disruption-puts-farmers-and-global-food-supplies-under-pressure</link><description>
As delegates gather in Turkey for the COP31 climate conference, discussions are focusing on emissions and climate targets. But humanitarian agencies are highlighting another urgent consequence of climate disruption: growing food insecurity. With the return of El Niño adding to concerns over extreme weather and its impact on food production, the Food and Agriculture Organisation is calling for food systems to be placed at the heart of climate action. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d0ad841e-de85-11f1-830b-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6146d7eb.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d0ad841e-de85-11f1-830b-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6146d7eb.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">61d9e6aa-de84-11f1-9697-7336d702d921</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:04:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>New restrictions to Starshield network 'kill more Ukrainians', Zelensky says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261112-new-systematic-restrictions-starshield-network-kill-more-ukrainians-zelensky-says</link><description>
Ukrainian ⁠President Volodymyr Zelensky ​on Thursday said that Ukrainian ​military units had recorded new and significant disruptions to the Starshield satellite communications service in recent days, affecting ​the ‌entire front ⁠line and Russian-occupied parts of Ukraine.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d00e4e44-de17-11f1-bda1-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-11T190959Z-1804496691-RC2ULOAAJ0M2-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-IRELAND.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d00e4e44-de17-11f1-bda1-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-11T190959Z-1804496691-RC2ULOAAJ0M2-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-IRELAND.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e1bb0658-de7d-11f1-9c1c-c333ff57169f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:06:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d00e4e44-de17-11f1-bda1-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-11T190959Z-1804496691-RC2ULOAAJ0M2-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-IRELAND.jpg">© Cathal McNaughton, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
